# Naming Conventions

All new folders and files must use proper PascalCase names. Never create lowercase, snake_case, or kebab-case names unless matching an existing numbered Source range pattern.

## Folders

- Use PascalCase: `Story`, `Notes`, `Chapters`, `References`, `Source`
- Bad: `story`, `notes`, `chapters`

## Files

- Use PascalCase for content files: `Races.md`, `Mounts.md`, `Creatures.md`
- Bad: `races.md`, `chapter-01.md`, `story_notes.md`
- Keep extensions lowercase: `.md`, `.py`, `.txt`
- Numbered Source ranges are allowed as-is: `1-10.md`, `101-110.md`

## When Creating or Renaming

- Match existing project casing exactly (Windows paths are case-insensitive; wrong casing still matters in the repo)
- To fix casing on Windows, rename via a temporary name first, then to the final PascalCase name
